cobit 19 infections and hospitalizations  have been dropping  nationally but some health experts  predict the worst weeks of the virus  might still be ahead  in nevada as elsewhere one of the key  tools in trying to control the spread  has been  contact tracing where those confirmed to  have copied  are contacted by health officials while  employees who have worked inside the  local program  say it is a miserable failure the  i-team's george knapp has our story  tens of thousands of eligible nevadans  have struggled to get appointments for a  cobit vaccination let alone get a second  shot  if you're wondering why the system is so  messed up the seeds may have been  planted  11 months ago when the health district  struggled to implement  basic plans including a program for  contact tracing  there's been so many delays where by the  time you reach people  that are positive it's already too late  they're already  well again and we can't even  begin to imagine how far it's spread to  other people until a few months ago john  worked for the southern nevada health  district as a contact tracer  each day he was assigned a file of 10 to  20 cases  people who had tested positive for covet  it was his job to contact the infected  person  and identify who else may have been  infected in practice he says  tracers were never able to finish their  daily lists  the delays between the time people were  tested and when they were informed of  the results grew from days  to weeks to a month or more sometimes we  had no idea  that the person has already died so  you're calling the family to tell them  hey you test positive  but they're already dead that's right  what's the reaction been like from the  family members  it's been a mix of anger sad  upset looking for someone to blame by  september john says the backlog for  contact tracers  was 15 thousand infected people who had  not been contacted  then it grew to 25 000. james is another  former health district employee  who confirmed the size of the backlog  and the chaos within the district um  it's just a disaster  it started from the beginning  where there just wasn't never enough  contact tracers  and once there's not enough contact  tracers  then it just gets more and more behind  and then it just becomes where contact  tracing  is useless contacting people  that showed positive a month ago  it doesn't do anything although contact  tracing has worked well in other  countries it's been a failure across  much of the u.s  in part because americans find it  intrusive or believe the virus is a hoax  or simply don't answer the phone  epidemiologist dr arturo moretto says  one reason the local health district  hasn't stood out as a miserable failure  is because so many other health  districts have done poorly as well  but you know it's leading good thing for  the health district the whole nation  is uh not you know doing well and that's  the only thing that is actually maybe  that they can use an excuse  arturo moretto spent almost 10 years  with the health district and specialized  in contact tracing  specifically for hiv cases it works he  says  but not as implemented for kovit many of  the senior managers at the district  were hired or promoted by former chief  joe iser  not for their expertise or training he  says but for their loyalty to icer  moreno says he discovered the district  making inflated claims to the state  about the success of its contact tracing  after he reported it to the state he was  fired because  they were claiming fifteen twenty  percent of the cases were being found  or identified through contact racing and  that was an absolute light moreto has  previous experience as a whistleblower  at the health district and has spoken  out about senior managers  lacking the most basic credentials for  dealing with infectious diseases  more on that in the days ahead george  knapp 8 news now  now george sought an interview with the  health district but the district  declined  a spokesperson did answer several  questions that we submitted in writing  saying the contact tracing program has  been able to quote  adequately respond to cobit except  during the summer surge of cases end  quote  you can read the full response on our  website
 

